      "worked": "Replace $x$ by $x+a$ so that the line $x=a$ becomes the new $y$-axis:\n$$y=f(x+a).$$\nReflect in the $y$-axis by replacing $x$ by $-x$:\n$$y=f(-x+a).$$\nTranslate back by replacing $x$ by $x-a$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=f(-(x-a)+a)\\\\y&=f(2a-x).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
